# VideoBrief — Product

Brand: **VideoBrief** · **Domain:** videobrief.app

**Contextual YouTube summarizer** — personalized section summaries synced with the video. Not a chatbot. Not education-first tooling.

## Core loop

Paste URL → **Preview** (metadata only; no DB row, no usage) → summary settings under the input (length + tone always; familiarity when YouTube category qualifies) → **Generate** → create library row + count usage + enqueue → **redirect to workspace** (job continues if user leaves) → worker fetches transcript → generate overview + sections **with bodies** → watch with sync highlight/seek.

## Guiding question

Does this help turn a YouTube video into a better personalized understanding for this user? If not, keep it out of MVP.

## MVP includes

Landing, auth (email/password + Google), soft email confirm, lightweight onboarding (optional default **tone** + **length** only), library with ephemeral preview → Generate, YouTube ingest (per-user `user_videos`; fetch transcript **from the analysis worker** on Generate), English timestamped captions, AI **generate only** (via `AIProvider`; **no classify stage**), per-video length/tone/familiarity (0–100) on the analysis row, video workspace with overview **summary** + section **bodies** + highlight/seek, dark-default UI, EN-only i18n scaffolding, unit tests, BullMQ analysis worker (Redis queue + usage counters).

## MVP excludes

Chat, uploads, Whisper/audio transcription, non-YouTube, recommendations, knowledge graph, cross-video search, quizzes, social/sharing, Stripe, tRPC, PostHog/analytics, E2E tests, non-English UI or captions (app DE + summary-language + non-EN transcripts = **post-MVP**), **LLM-invented knowledge questions**, topic/video EAV context, shared cross-user transcript cache, AI classify / `isEducational` / non-edu disclaimer, educational profile fields (YOB, education level, subjects).

Redis is **queue + per-video lock + usage counters** (not a transcript cache).

## UX

Editorial, premium, content-first, typography-led. AI stays invisible in the workspace. Prefer Watch → understand → remember over chat.

## Context rules

- Onboarding stays lightweight; every field optional. Skip → defaults **tone 50**, **length 50**.
- Profile defaults (typed): `summary_tone` (0–100), `summary_length` (0–100). No YOB / education / subjects / `summary_style` enum.
- Per-video prefs on the **analysis row**: `summary_length`, `summary_tone`, `familiarity` (nullable). Slider ends: length Short←→Long; tone **Formal←→Casual**; familiarity Novice←→Expert (copy TBD). Defaults from profile (or 50/50).
- Familiarity shown only when YouTube category is one of: Education, Howto & Style, Science & Technology, News & Politics (fixed category-id map; may extend later). Otherwise omit from UI and generate prompt.
- Preview is ephemeral (client + read-only preview action). **No** `user_videos` / analysis row until Generate. Abandon = nothing to delete.
- Re-Generate / same URL again → **reset** (new `run_id`, clear prior summary/sections).
- Generate emits `{ summary, sections: { title, startTime, endTime, body }[] }`. No classify stage.
